  },
  "note": "Annual election of the Aughnacloy Town Commissioners, polled Friday 15 January 1932. Only seven candidates were nominated for nine seats; Rea and George Wright were declared elected to the two remaining vacancies, so there was no contest (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1932, p. 2). Five outgoing Unionists, two Nationalists (Brady outgoing, M'Quade new), with Rea and Wright filling the last two seats. Returned unopposed."
